# `.mjs` is always source text, so diff it as text (#1897).
#
# Git calls a blob binary when it finds a NUL byte in the first 8000, and
# scripts/ci/money-path.test.mjs had two — a literal NUL used as a regex
# placeholder. The effect was that the drift guard for the MONEY PATH was the
# one file in the repository that showed up as `Bin 10325 -> 16418 bytes`
# instead of a diff, so no pull request touching it could be reviewed by
# reading the change. #1897 rewrote that byte as a `\u0000` escape; this line
# also makes the diff readable across the commit that still has the old blob
# on one side, and keeps the class of failure from recurring silently.
#
# `diff` only affects how git renders changes. It is not `text`, so no
# line-ending normalisation is implied.
*.mjs diff
